module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.Transform.CartierCentre
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.IdealSheafSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.Flattening.AffineChartDescent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.RaynaudGrusonFlattening0815

/-!
# The unit centre, and what `AffineChartFlatteningCentre` asks at `U = ⊤`

`AlgebraicGeometry.AffineChartFlatteningCentre f F U`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Flatness/Flattening/AffineChartDescent.lean`) is the predicate
the formalized forms of [Stacks, Tags 0815, 081R, 081S, 081T, 0B49, 0CP1, 0EVC, 0F3W, 0F3Z] carry.
It imposes no hypothesis on `f`, `F` or `U`. This file determines it completely at `U = ⊤`:
there it is *equivalent* to `F` being flat over the base already.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_blowUpToBase_top`: the blowup in the unit ideal sheaf is an
  isomorphism — [Stacks, Tag 0807] at the unit ideal, which is an effective Cartier divisor.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatOver_of_isFlatOver_strictTransformSheaf_top`: if the strict transform
  of `F` in the unit centre is flat over the blowup, then `F` is flat over the base. This is the
  converse of `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatOver_strictTransformSheaf_of_isFlatOver` at the unit
  centre, and it holds because at that centre the blowup is an isomorphism and the strict
  transform is the plain pullback.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.affineChartFlatteningCentre_top_iff`:
  `AffineChartFlatteningCentre f F ⊤ ↔ IsFlatOver f F`.

## What this settles

`AlgebraicGeometry.AffineChartFlatteningCentre.of_isFlatOver` produces the predicate from
flatness of `F` over the base. The equivalence below says that at `U = ⊤` that producer is not
merely the region currently reachable — it is the *only* region there is. So no producer of the
predicate can drop the flatness hypothesis in that generality, and in particular the predicate
is false whenever `F` is not flat over the base: take `f` the identity of `Spec k[x, y]` and
`F = 𝒪/(x)`.

This matters because the declarations carrying the predicate drop hypotheses of their sources
into it — hypotheses (2)-(5) of [Stacks, Tag 0815] for
`AlgebraicGeometry.AffineChartFlatteningCentre.exists_isAdmissibleBlowup_isFlatOver`,
and hypothesis (2) of [Stacks, Tag 081R], that `X_U ⟶ U` be flat and locally of finite
presentation, for `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAdmissibleBlowup_flat_strictTransform` — on the
ground that they enter the source's proof only through the affine case. They do, but the
predicate does not re-impose them, and the flatness hypothesis is exactly what the equivalence
below shows cannot be dropped. Proving the affine case of [Stacks, Tag 0815] therefore will not
discharge the predicate as it stands; the predicate has to carry the chart-level forms of its
source's hypotheses first.

At `U = ⊤` this is not an artefact of the formalization: the source's hypothesis (5) at `U = ⊤`
*is* flatness of `F` over all of `S`, and `Stacks.Blowup.eq_top_of_disjoint_univ_support` says
the unit ideal sheaf is the only `⊤`-admissible centre, so at `U = ⊤` [Stacks, Tag 0815] itself
asserts nothing beyond its hypothesis. The content of the equivalence is that the predicate,
asked without that hypothesis, is not weaker.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0815](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0815)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0807](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0807)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 080F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/080F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02JZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02JZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05B9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05B9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **The blowup in the unit ideal sheaf is an isomorphism.** The unit ideal sheaf is an
effective Cartier divisor — locally it is generated by the nonzerodivisor `1` — so this is
[Stacks, Tag 0807]. -/
theorem isIso_blowUpToBase_top {S : Scheme.{u}} :
    IsIso (blowUpToBase (⊤ : S.IdealSheafData)) :=
  isIso_blowUpToBase_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor ⊤
    Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_top

/-- **The strict transform in the unit centre is the plain pullback.** The exceptional divisor of
the blowup in the unit ideal sheaf is empty, so no sections are divided out and the quotient map
of [Stacks, Tag 080F] part (2) is an isomorphism with no flatness hypothesis at all. -/
theorem isIso_strictTransformSheaf_quotient_top {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] :
    IsIso (Stacks.StrictTransform.π f (blowUpToBase (⊤ : S.IdealSheafData))
      (exceptionalIdeal (⊤ : S.IdealSheafData)) F) :=
  isIso_strictTransformSheaf_quotient_of_flat_at_exceptional f ⊤ F fun x hx ↦ by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_top, ← SetLike.mem_coe,
      TopologicalSpace.Closeds.coe_bot, Set.mem_empty_iff_false] at hx
    exact hx.elim

/-- **The converse of `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatOver_strictTransformSheaf_of_isFlatOver` at the
unit centre.** If the strict transform of `F` in the unit ideal sheaf is flat over the blowup,
then `F` is flat over the base.

The blowup is an isomorphism (`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_blowUpToBase_top`), so the projection
`pr_X : X ×_S S' ⟶ X` is an isomorphism too, hence flat and surjective; the strict transform is
the pullback of `F` along it (`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_strictTransformSheaf_quotient_top`); and
pullback along a flat surjection detects flatness over a base ([Stacks, Tag 02JZ]), the
remaining isomorphism of bases being absorbed by [Stacks, Tag 05B9]. -/
theorem isFlatOver_of_isFlatOver_strictTransformSheaf_top {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (h : IsFlatOver (pullback.snd f (blowUpToBase (⊤ : S.IdealSheafData))).toLRSHom.toShHom
      (Stacks.StrictTransform.sheaf f (blowUpToBase (⊤ : S.IdealSheafData))
        (exceptionalIdeal (⊤ : S.IdealSheafData)) F)) :
    IsFlatOver f.toLRSHom.toShHom F := by
  have : IsIso (blowUpToBase (⊤ : S.IdealSheafData)) := isIso_blowUpToBase_top
  have hπ := isIso_strictTransformSheaf_quotient_top f F
  set b := blowUpToBase (⊤ : S.IdealSheafData)
  set p := pullback.fst f b
  set q := pullback.snd f b
  have : IsIso p := inferInstanceAs (IsIso (pullback.fst f b))
  let Fm : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) := F
  have : Fm.IsQuasicoherent := ‹F.IsQuasicoherent›
  have : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback p).obj F).IsQuasicoherent :=
    @AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.modulePullback_isQuasicoherent _ _
      p.toLRSHom.toShHom F ‹F.IsQuasicoherent›
  have h1 : IsFlatOver q.toLRSHom.toShHom ((Scheme.Modules.pullback p).obj F) :=
    fun y ↦ isFlatOverAt_of_moduleIso _ (@asIso _ _ _ _ _ hπ).symm y (h y)
  have h2 : IsFlatOver (q ≫ b).toLRSHom.toShHom ((Scheme.Modules.pullback p).obj F) :=
    fun y ↦ (isFlatOverAt_comp_iff_of_etale q b _ y).mpr (h1 y)
  rw [isFlatOver_iff_modulePullback_isFlatOver p f Fm,
    show p ≫ f = q ≫ b from pullback.condition]
  exact h2

/-- **At `U = ⊤` the carried affine case of [Stacks, Tag 0815] is flatness over the base.**

One direction is `AlgebraicGeometry.AffineChartFlatteningCentre.of_isFlatOver`. For the other,
`Stacks.Blowup.eq_top_of_disjoint_univ_support` forces the centre supplied on each chart to be
the unit ideal sheaf, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatOver_of_isFlatOver_strictTransformSheaf_top` then turns the flatness of
its strict transform into flatness of `F` on the chart; flatness over a base is checked one
point at a time, and every point of `X` lies on such a chart.

No hypothesis is needed on `f`, on `F` beyond quasi-coherence, or on `S`. -/
theorem affineChartFlatteningCentre_top_iff {S X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (F : X.Modules)
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] :
    AffineChartFlatteningCentre f F ⊤ ↔ IsFlatOver f.toLRSHom.toShHom F := by
  refine ⟨fun H x ↦ ?_, fun hF ↦ AffineChartFlatteningCentre.of_isFlatOver f F ⊤ hF⟩
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, -⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (show f x ∈ (⊤ : S.Opens) from trivial)
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, hWV⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (show x ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V from hxV)
  obtain ⟨I, -, hdisj, hflat⟩ := H ⟨V, hV⟩ ⟨W, hW⟩ hWV
  obtain rfl : I = ⊤ :=
    Stacks.Blowup.eq_top_of_disjoint_univ_support (by simpa using hdisj)
  have : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback W.ι).obj F).IsQuasicoherent :=
    Stacks.Modules.isQuasicoherent_pullback W.ι F ‹_›
  have hres : IsFlatOver (f.resLE V W hWV).toLRSHom.toShHom
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback W.ι).obj F) :=
    isFlatOver_of_isFlatOver_strictTransformSheaf_top _ _ hflat
  have hW' : IsFlatAt W.ι.toLRSHom.toShHom (⟨x, hxW⟩ : W.toScheme) :=
    Flat.stalkMap W.ι ⟨x, hxW⟩
  refine (isFlatOverAt_iff_modulePullback_isFlatOverAt W.ι f F ⟨x, hxW⟩ hW').mpr ?_
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.resLE_comp_ι f hWV]
  exact (isFlatOverAt_comp_iff_of_etale (f.resLE V W hWV) V.ι
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback W.ι).obj F) ⟨x, hxW⟩).mpr (hres ⟨x, hxW⟩)

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
